The '''Aston Martin One-77''' is a two-door, two-seater flagship [[sports car]] built by the British car manufacturer [[Aston Martin]]. The car was first shown at the [[2008 Paris Motor Show]], although it remained mostly covered by a "[[Savile Row]] tailored skirt" throughout the show.<ref name=edmunds2>{{cite web|url=http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/autoshows/paris/2008/astonmartinone77.html#astonne772 |title=Aston Martin One-77 – 2008 Paris Auto Show |publisher=Edmunds.com |access-date=18 July 2009 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090206151038/http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/autoshows/paris/2008/astonmartinone77.html |archive-date=6 February 2009 |df=dmy }}</ref> It was revealed in full at the [[Geneva Motor Show#2009|2009 Geneva Motor Show]], and deliveries began in 2011.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-culture/buying-maintenance/news/a32558/aston-martin-one-77-for-sale-price/|title = Extremely Rare Aston Martin One-77 for Sale for Unknown Millions of Dollars|date = 8 February 2017}}</ref>

The production of the One-77 was limited to 77 cars, although several development cars were made for engineering, testing, and marketing.  One of the development cars, VIN #10711 was sent back to Aston Martin for complete refurbishment, and now is owned under [[National Highway Traffic Safety Administration]] (NHTSA) [[Show or Display]] registration in the United States, making the actual total of cars in existence to be 78.  The car's development formed part of the name One-77,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/do/News/articleId=130447#2 |title=2008 Paris Auto Show Preview: Aston Martin One-77 |publisher=Edmunds.com |date=8 August 2008 |access-date=18 July 2009 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090307054454/http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/do/News/articleId%3D130447 |archive-date=7 March 2009 |df=dmy }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.motorauthority.com/news/concept-cars/limited-edition-aston-martin-one-77-preview-leaked/ |title=Live shots of Aston Martin's One-77 supercar – [2010 Aston Martin One-77 supercar&#93; – MotorAuthority – Car news, reviews, spy shots |publisher=MotorAuthority |access-date=18 July 2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081202232440/http://www.motorauthority.com/news/concept-cars/limited-edition-aston-martin-one-77-preview-leaked/ |archive-date=2 December 2008 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref> and sold for {{GBP}}1,150,000.<ref>{{cite web|last=Metcalfe|first=Harry|title=Aston Martin One-77|url=http://www.autoexpress.co.uk/aston-martin/one-77/62239/aston-martin-one-77-driven|work=Auto Express|access-date=11 April 2013|date=16 January 2013}}</ref> In May 2012, one of the 77 cars was involved in a crash in Hong Kong and was initially written off,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.motorauthority.com/news/1076514_hong-kong-witnesses-first-aston-martin-one-77-crash |title=Hong Kong Witnesses First Aston Martin One-77 Crash |publisher=MotorAuthority.com |date= 27 May 2012}}</ref> but has since been  fully rebuilt.

==Specifications==
[[File:2012 Aston Martin One-77 7.3 Rear.jpg|left|thumb|Rear view]]
[[File:Interior of Aston Martin One77.jpg|thumb|Interior|left]]
Prior to the One-77's Paris Motor Show debut, various details about the car were revealed,<ref name="autogenerated1">[http://925.nl/archief/2008/09/29/925-wereldprimeur-fotos-en-specs-van-aston-martin-project-aston-/ 925 wereldprimeur: Foto's en specs van Aston Martin Project Aston One-77] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110724055721/http://925.nl/archief/2008/09/29/925-wereldprimeur-fotos-en-specs-van-aston-martin-project-aston-/ |date=24 July 2011 }} (Dutch) [https://translate.google.com/translate?u=http%3A%2F%2F925.nl%2Farchief%2F2008%2F09%2F29%2F925-wereldprimeur-fotos-en-specs-van-aston-martin-project-aston-&sl=nl&tl=en&hl=en&ie=UTF-8 Google translation]</ref> but official specifications were not fully revealed until the [[Geneva Motor Show#2009|2009 Geneva Motor Show]].

The One-77 features a full [[Carbon fiber reinforced polymer#Automotive engineering|carbon fibre]] monocoque chassis, a handcrafted aluminium body, and a {{cvt|7312|cc|L CID|1|abbr=on|order=flip}} [[Overhead camshaft#Dual overhead camshaft|DOHC]], four valve per cylinder [[V12 engine]] with [[variable valve timing]] rated at {{Convert|559|kW|PS hp|0|abbr=on}} at 7,500 rpm and {{Convert|750|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque at 5,000 rpm. [[Aston Martin]] claimed the engine to be the most powerful production naturally aspirated engine in the world when the first car was delivered.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.astonmartin.com/thecompany/news?a=d56b5dd1-8a66-4ef8-b8ff-4e3b1799a45a |title=Aston Martin One-77: Featuring the World's Most Powerful Naturally Aspirated Road Car Engine. |publisher=Astonmartin.com |date=21 September 2010 |access-date=20 March 2011 }}{{Dead link|date=September 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

The car utilises a 6-speed [[automated manual transmission]] from [[Graziano Trasmissioni]] and height-adjustable pushrod suspension coupled with dynamic [[Electronic stability control|stability control]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/autoshows/paris/2008/astonmartinone77detailsleaknews.html |title=2008 Paris Auto Show Preview: Aston Martin One-77 Details Leak on the Web |publisher=Edmunds.com |date=22 January 2009 |access-date=20 March 2011 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090729101047/http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/autoshows/paris/2008/astonmartinone77detailsleaknews.html |archive-date=29 July 2009 |df=dmy }}</ref> The One-77 features [[Pirelli]] P Zero Corsa tyres (255/35 ZR20 front, 335/30 ZR20 rear) and Carbon Ceramic Matrix brakes.

The top speed was estimated to be {{convert|217|mi/h|km/h|abbr=on|order=flip}} but actual tests in December 2009 showed a figure of {{convert|220.007|mi/h|km/h|abbr=on|order=flip}},<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.astonmartin.com/thecompany/news?a=1c7926f7-54c9-44a7-bd09-b720f6b59509 |title=One-77 closes on new Aston Martin record |date=22 December 2009 |work=astonmartin.com |publisher=Aston Martin |access-date=18 February 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100130035153/http://www.astonmartin.com/thecompany/news?a=1c7926f7-54c9-44a7-bd09-b720f6b59509 |archive-date=30 January 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref> with a 0–{{convert|97|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} acceleration time of approximately 3.5 seconds.

The engineering and manufacturing of the carbon fibre chassis and suspension system was contracted to [[Multimatic]] of Canada. The projected weight was {{convert|1500|kg|lb|0|abbr=on}},<ref>{{cite web|last=Abuelsamid |first=Sam |url=http://www.autoblog.com/2009/03/03/geneva-2009-aston-martin-one-77-almost-fully-revealed/ |title=Geneva 2009: Aston Martin One-77 almost fully revealed |publisher=Autoblog.com |date=3 March 2009 |access-date=20 March 2011}}</ref> but the production model weighs {{Convert|1630|kg|lb|0|abbr=on}}.

==Accolades==

The Aston Martin One-77 has been awarded with several internationally renowned design awards including the [[Concorso d'Eleganza Villa d'Este|Concorso d’Eleganza]] Design Award for Concept Cars and Prototypes,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://site.astonmartin.com/eng/thecompany/news?a=aef9fefe-d985-4e21-920d-708f86120c96 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20120714180751/http://site.astonmartin.com/eng/thecompany/news?a=aef9fefe-d985-4e21-920d-708f86120c96 |url-status=dead |archive-date=14 July 2012 |title=Aston Martin One-77 wins top design award at the Concorso d'Eleganza, Villa d'Este |publisher=AstonMartin.com |date=26 April 2009 }}</ref> the [[Good Design Award (Chicago)|GOOD DESIGN]] award by The Chicago Athenauem: Museum of Architecture and Design in North America<ref>{{cite web|url=http://site.astonmartin.com/eng/thecompany/news?a=fa5d6c7a-bc9b-4372-b74d-0e399eaffed7 |title=One-77 Bestowed with Prestigious Design Award |publisher=AstonMartin.com |date=11 January 2009 }}{{dead link|date=October 2016 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> and the "Best Design" award by the UK motoring magazine [[Auto Express]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://site.astonmartin.com/eng/thecompany/news?a=55cdf09e-cf2d-41b2-b353-f86e3f9b66e1 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20120720184853/http://site.astonmartin.com/eng/thecompany/news?a=55cdf09e-cf2d-41b2-b353-f86e3f9b66e1 |url-status=dead |archive-date=20 July 2012 |title=Aston Martin One-77 Wins Design Award |publisher=AstonMartin.com |date=6 August 2009 }}</ref> and many others.

==One-77 "Q-Series"==
Towards the end of its production, Aston Martin produced a seven-unit, special version of the One-77 called the "Q-Series". The "Q" part of the name comes from the Q by Aston Martin personalisation program. The "series" part of the name is a possible reference to the selection of liveries that appear on each car.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.topspeed.com/cars/aston-martin/2013-aston-martin-one-77-q-series-by-aston-martin-ar134611.html|title=2013 Aston Martin One-77 Q-Series by Aston Martin|date=6 September 2012|publisher=TopSpeed.com|access-date=23 January 2017}}{{dead link|date=January 2025|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref>

The vehicle liveries are:
* Metallic grey paint, black 10-spoke wheels, red/black two-tone interior, red stripe on the front fascia
* Solid white paint, silver 10-spoke wheels, black interior, red stripe on the front fascia, black wing mirrors
* Solid white paint, silver 12-spoke wheels, red/black two-tone interior, red double stripe along the body
* Black paint, black 10-spoke wheels, red/black two-tone interior, red stripe on the front fascia, dark red wing mirrors

The specifications and performance figures are the same as the regular car. One of these vehicles was on sale in 2012 in Dubai for AED 11 million (US$2.9 million).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://luxatic.com/aston-martin-one-77-q-series-for-sale-in-dubai-for-3m/|title=Aston Martin One-77 Q-Series For Sale in Dubai For 3M|date=12 September 2012|publisher=Luxatic.com|access-date=23 January 2017}}</ref>

== Aston Martin Victor ==
In September 2020, Aston Martin launched its coach-built model based on the One-77, the '''Aston Martin Victor''', designed by Aston Martin Lagonda designer Kaize "Ken" Zheng and unveiled at Hampton Courts Concours 2020 with circular-shaped headlights meant to evoke those of the 1977 [[Aston Martin V8 Vantage (1977)|Aston Martin V8 Vantage]], side exhausts and side bumpers reused from the track-only [[Aston Martin Vulcan|Vulcan]]. It has a similar engine as the V12 found in the One-77 but it now makes {{cvt|836|bhp|kW|0}} and {{cvt|606|lbft|Nm|0}} of torque after being revised by [[Cosworth]], and unlike the One-77, it has a manual transmission, which made it the most powerful Aston Martin with a manual transmission at the time.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-09-04|title=The Aston Martin Victor is an 836bhp manual masterpiece|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/british/aston-martin-victor-836bhp-manual-masterpiece|access-date=2021-02-01|website=Top Gear|language=en}}</ref><gallery widths="220" heights="140">
